cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the paper
  "Confidence Intervals and Simultaneous Bands for Additive-Hazards Sequential
  Trial Emulation" (M. Ehsan Karim).
type: software
title: >-
  steCI: Confidence Intervals and Simultaneous Bands for Additive-Hazards
  Sequential Trial Emulation
version: 0.0.1
authors:
  - family-names: Karim
    given-names: M. Ehsan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0346-2871"
    affiliation: >-
      School of Population and Public Health, University of British Columbia,
      Vancouver, Canada
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ehsanx/steCI"
abstract: >-
  R package steCI and the reproducibility compendium of its companion paper.
  The package estimates a constant hazard difference and the marginal
  risk-difference curve by sequential trial emulation with a weighted Aalen
  additive-hazards model and stabilised inverse-probability-of-artificial-censoring
  weights, and provides model-based, row-level robust and subject-clustered
  analytic standard errors, the nonparametric bootstrap, the jackknife, and a
  multiplier bootstrap with pointwise intervals and a simultaneous sup-t band
  for the risk-difference curve.
keywords:
  - sequential trial emulation
  - additive hazards
  - Aalen model
  - confidence intervals
  - simultaneous confidence bands
  - multiplier bootstrap
  - cluster-robust variance
  - influence function
  - survival analysis
  - R
